(* precise.pvl
   A setting of ProVerif for the variants whose attacks the prover must rebuild as a trace (AUD-6, #409). Since the
   responder takes the static key of any initiator, the first derivations that ProVerif finds of some attacks of
   quic-cert, nobinding-cert and neither-none rest on an approximation of the actions of a process, and their traces
   cannot be rebuilt: the answer is "cannot be proved" where the attack is real. With preciseActions the prover keeps the
   actions of each process apart, finds the derivations of the real attacks and rebuilds them, at about four times the
   time of the variant (under a minute). A variant takes this file first. *)

set preciseActions = true.
